Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: tdesktop_rust
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop/issues
Source: https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop
Comment:
 There is no upstream release of tdesktop_rust: Telegram Desktop's build
 recipes generate it as a two-line umbrella crate over tlottie and
 wallet-engine, which this package carries as submodules at the commits
 Telegram Desktop pins.
 .
 vendor/ holds the crates.io dependencies of both, and of the
 uniffi-bindgen-cpp generator, each with its own licence files in place. The
 licences below are the ones each crate declares in its Cargo.toml. The
 crates no Linux amd64/arm64 build reaches are source-less stubs, generated
 by cargo vendor-filterer, containing only their manifest; they are covered
 by the vendor/* paragraph.
 .
 The static library links the Rust standard library, which is distributed
 under the MIT or Apache-2.0 terms; only its object code, not its source,
 ends up in the binary package.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026, Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>
License: MIT

Files: tlottie/*
Copyright: 2026, dkaraush <dkaraush@gmail.com>
License: MIT

Files: wallet-engine/*
Copyright: 2026, TON Core
License: Apache-2.0 or MIT

Files: wallet-engine/vendor/ton/*
Copyright: Sild <silddev@pm.com>
License: Apache-2.0 or MIT
Comment: ston-fi/ton-rs, vendored by wallet-engine itself.

Files: wallet-engine/bindgen/cpp/*
Copyright: Nord Security and the uniffi-bindgen-cpp contributors
License: MPL-2.0
Comment: NordSecurity/uniffi-bindgen-cpp, vendored by wallet-engine itself.
 It generates wallet_engine.hpp and wallet_engine.cpp from its templates, so
 the generated binding shipped in the binary package is covered by the same
 licence.

Files: debian/patches/wallet-engine.patch
Copyright: 2026, John Preston <johnprestonmail@gmail.com>
License: Apache-2.0 or MIT
Comment: Unmodified from desktop-app/patches, the patch set Telegram Desktop
 applies to its dependencies. It changes wallet-engine and is distributed
 under wallet-engine's terms.

